    "applicationMode": "Online through the National Testing Agency (NTA) SHRESHTA/NETS application and counselling process. The student first applies for and takes the National Entrance Test for SHRESHTA; selected students then participate in web counselling to select from available Ministry-approved SHRESHTA schools. The school-fee payment is released directly by the Ministry to the selected school through the Ministry’s e-Anudaan portal.",
    "officialApplyLink": "UNCONFIRMED — needs current-cycle verification. The official guideline establishes NETS as the student-selection route but does not contain a permanent live application URL. Check the  National Testing Agency website [ https://nta.ac.in/ ] for the active SHRESHTA/NETS notice and application link when the examination cycle opens.",
    "verificationSourceLink": "https://socialjustice.gov.in/schemes/41\n\n\nhttps://socialjustice.gov.in/public/ckeditor/upload/24291692705460.pdf",
    "applicationWindow": "Check the NTA SHRESHTA/NETS portal for the current cycle. The guidelines do not establish fixed student-application months. For reference only, the official 2025 material shows counselling registration and choice filling from 28 June to 4 July 2025, but this must not be treated as the 2026-27 timetable.",
    "lastVerifiedDate": "24 August 2026",
    "researcher": "Sugandhi",
    "notesFlags": "The Ministry page and guideline located cover 2023-24 to 2025-26. A current 2026-27 continuation, revised benefit limits, updated school list, NETS notification, application dates, and active direct-apply URL must be verified before publishing a live link in the app. SHRESHTA has two modes: Mode 1 is the student-facing NETS route into selected private residential schools; Mode 2 funds continuing eligible NGO/voluntary-organisation schools, hostels, and projects. This row is written mainly for Mode 1, because it is the direct student-discovery/applicant pathway. Do not present Mode 2 as a student scholarship application—the applicant there is the eligible NGO/VO, not an individual student. The scholarship amount is paid to the school, not deposited into the student’s account. The student must not simultaneously be covered under the Department’s Pre-Matric Scholarship Scheme.",
