    "categoryLabel": "ST",
    "educationLevel": "Class 11-12 / UG / PG / Diploma / PhD (the 2022 guideline describes support from Class XI to postgraduate courses; it also classifies recognised M.Phil./PhD courses for benefit purposes. However, verify actual current PhD coverage against the State/UT portal because a separate National Fellowship for ST Students also exists.)",
    "incomeCeiling": "₹2,50,000 per year total family income from all sources. Exception: for an orphan supported by a guardian, the income criterion does not apply.",
    "incomeLimit": 250000,
    "officialEligibility": "The applicant must belong to a Scheduled Tribe specified for the State/UT of their domicile. The student must have passed Matriculation, Higher Secondary, or a higher examination from a recognised board or university and must be pursuing a recognised post-matriculation or post-secondary course in India. Family income from all sources must not exceed ₹2.5 lakh annually, except in the case of an orphan supported by a guardian. The applicant must hold a valid bank account in a scheduled bank linked with Aadhaar and a mobile number. The student cannot receive another scholarship or stipend at the same time; if awarded another one, they must choose one. The applicant may study at an eligible Government institution anywhere in India, or at a non-Government institution empanelled by the State/UT of domicile. Students newly admitted to the Ministry’s notified Top Class institutions are not eligible for this PMS-ST scheme because they are to be covered by the separate National Scholarship for Higher Education of ST Students/Top Class scheme.",
    "plainEligibility": "This scholarship is for ST students whose family earns up to ₹2.5 lakh a year and who are studying after Class 10 in a recognised course in India, such as Class 11-12, college, diploma, ITI, or postgraduate study. You apply through the State/UT where you are officially a resident, need an Aadhaar-linked bank account, and usually cannot receive another scholarship at the same time.",
    "benefits": "Two parts: eligible compulsory non-refundable course fees plus a monthly stipend. Fee support: The State/UT fixes the approved fee amount. For students admitted from 1 April 2022 onward to private institutions, the Central Government support ceiling is: ₹2.5 lakh/year for engineering, ₹6 lakh/year for MBBS/MS/MD, and ₹1 lakh/year for other courses. A State/UT may provide additional support above these limits from its own funds. Monthly stipend, paid for up to 10 months each academic year: - Group I — professional degree, postgraduate degree/diploma, M.Phil./PhD: ₹1,200/month hosteller; ₹550/month day scholar. - Group II — non-professional recognised UG/PG courses, such as BA/BSc/BCom or MA/MSc/MCom: ₹820/month hosteller; ₹530/month day scholar. - Group III — vocational, ITI, and three-year polytechnic diploma courses: ₹570/month hosteller; ₹300/month day scholar. - Group IV — Class 11-12 and other post-matric non-degree courses where Class 10 is the entry qualification: ₹380/month hosteller; ₹230/month day scholar. Additional disability allowance: ₹800/month for an eligible Divyang hosteller or ₹600/month for an eligible Divyang day scholar, in addition to the normal stipend. This additional allowance also applies to eligible leprosy-cured students and students with sickle-cell anaemia or thalassaemia, subject to the guideline’s certification rules.",
