    "applicationMode": "Online through the relevant State/UT scholarship portal or National Scholarship Portal (NSP), depending on the applicant’s domicile State/UT. The State/UT processes, verifies, and awards the scholarship; the Ministry of Tribal Affairs releases the Central share to the State/UT.",
    "officialApplyLink": "https://scholarships.gov.in/All-Scholarships \n\n\nImportant: This scheme is State/UT-administered. If your domicile State/UT has its own PMS-ST portal, apply through that official State/UT portal instead of assuming NSP is the active route.",
    "verificationSourceLink": "https://scholarships.gov.in/public/schemeGuidelines/Post-matric-guidelines-ST.pdf \n\n\nhttps://scholarships.gov.in/public/schemeGuidelines/Post-matric-guidelines-ST.pdf",
    "applicationWindow": "The PMS-ST guideline gives a suggested annual registration window of 1 April to 30 September for both fresh and renewal applicants. States/UTs are advised to open their portals by 1 May. Check the relevant State/UT or NSP portal for the live deadline, because these timelines are expressly described as suggestive.",
