    "notesFlags": "The main official guideline is applicable from 1 April 2022 and its stated main scope is Class XI to postgraduate study, although its benefit table includes M.Phil./PhD course categories. Your original wording “Class 11 onwards to PhD” should therefore be flagged for current-cycle confirmation, especially because the Ministry also runs a separate National Fellowship for ST Students (NFST) for research scholars. Students newly admitted to Ministry-notified Top Class institutions are not eligible for PMS-ST under the 2022 guideline; they should use the separate Top Class ST scholarship route. The direct application route varies by State/UT; do not promise NSP as the only application link. The ₹2.5 lakh income ceiling, course-group stipend rates, and private-institution fee ceilings should be checked against the live State/UT portal before public release because States/UTs may have implementation-specific procedures and may provide extra support above central ceilings.",
