    "officialEligibility": "The applicant must belong to a Scheduled Tribe specified for the State/UT of their domicile. The student must be studying in Class IX or X in a Government school or a school recognised by the Government or a Central/State Board of Secondary Education. Family income from all sources must not exceed ₹2.5 lakh per year, except for an orphan supported by a guardian. The student must have a valid bank account in a scheduled bank linked with Aadhaar and mobile number. The student must not be receiving any other scholarship. Scholarship for the same class is available for only one year; a student who repeats a class cannot receive it again for that class. Renewal for Class X is possible after passing Class IX, subject to good conduct and regular attendance.",
    "plainEligibility": "This scholarship is for ST students in Class 9 or Class 10 whose family earns up to ₹2.5 lakh a year. You must study in a recognised school, have an Aadhaar-linked bank account, and not already receive another scholarship; if you repeat the same class, you cannot receive the award twice for that class.",
    "benefits": "Paid for 10 months in an academic year: - Day scholar: ₹225 per month = ₹2,250/year, plus ₹750/year books and ad hoc grant = ₹3,000/year total. - Hosteller: ₹525 per month = ₹5,250/year, plus ₹1,000/year books and ad hoc grant = ₹6,250/year total. Additional disability allowance: ₹800/month for an eligible hosteller with disability, or ₹600/month for an eligible day scholar with disability. This additional allowance is payable for all 12 months of the year. It also applies to eligible leprosy-cured students and students with sickle-cell anaemia or thalassaemia, subject to certification by the competent medical authority. The scholarship is transferred directly to the student’s bank account through DBT after verification by the school and State/UT authorities.",
