    "categoryLabel": "ST",
    "educationLevel": "UG / PG / PhD (officially, the scholarship component covers graduate and postgraduate study at Ministry-notified institutions; the fellowship component supports full-time M.Phil./PhD research after postgraduate study. For a 2026 app, display PhD with a verification flag because current M.Phil. admissions and current fellowship implementation need confirmation.)",
    "incomeCeiling": "₹6,00,000 per year total family income from all sources — applies to the Scholarship/Top Class Education component only.\n\nFellowship component: No family-income ceiling is stated in the official guideline reviewed.",
    "incomeLimit": 600000,
    "officialEligibility": "Scholarship component: The applicant must belong to the Scheduled Tribe category, secure admission according to the admission rules of a Ministry of Tribal Affairs–notified institution, and pursue a full-time eligible graduate or postgraduate course. Total family income from all sources must not exceed ₹6 lakh per year. The scholarship begins after admission and class attendance start, and continues for the course duration subject to satisfactory performance. Fellowship component: The applicant must belong to the Scheduled Tribe category, have passed postgraduate study, and obtain admission and registration in a regular, full-time M.Phil./PhD programme at an eligible UGC-recognised, Government-funded, Institute of National Importance, or other Ministry-identified academic/research institution. A fellow cannot receive another Central or State Government scholarship for the same study. Fellowship payment starts only after admission, registration, and commencement of research work.",
    "plainEligibility": "This scheme has two routes for ST students. If you get into a Government-notified top college for an undergraduate or postgraduate course and your family earns up to ₹6 lakh a year, you may qualify for the scholarship route. If you have completed postgraduate study and are starting a full-time PhD or other eligible research programme at an approved institution, you may qualify for the fellowship route; the official guideline does not set an income limit for that route.",
    "benefits": "Scholarship/Top Class component: - Full tuition fee and other compulsory non-refundable fees at Government/Government-funded institutions. - At private institutions: tuition fee support up to ₹2,50,000 per year per student. - Books and stationery: ₹3,000 per year. - Living expenses: ₹2,200 per month, up to ₹26,400 per year. - Computer and accessories: up to ₹45,000 as one-time assistance during the course. Fellowship component: - M.Phil. fellowship: ₹25,000 per month, for up to 2 years or until dissertation submission, whichever is earlier. - PhD fellowship: ₹28,000 per month, for up to 5 years or until viva voce, whichever is earlier. - Annual contingency: Humanities/Social Sciences — ₹10,000 for M.Phil. and ₹20,500 for PhD; Science/Engineering/Technology — ₹12,000 for M.Phil. and ₹25,000 for PhD. - HRA as per the relevant university/institution rules. - Reader/escort assistance: ₹2,000 per month for eligible physically disabled and blind fellows. Scholarship payments are made yearly; fellowship payments are made quarterly through DBT to the Aadhaar-seeded bank account.",
