    "plainEligibility": "This fellowship is for ST students who have finished postgraduation with at least 55% marks, cleared UGC-NET or CSIR-NET, and are doing a regular full-time PhD at an approved Indian university or research institution. You cannot take another government scholarship or fellowship for the same course at the same time.",
    "benefits": "Monthly fellowship: - PhD: ₹28,000 per month, payable for up to 5 years or until thesis submission, whichever is earlier. - M.Phil. under the historic guideline: ₹25,000 per month, payable for up to 2 years or until dissertation submission, whichever is earlier. Annual contingency grant: - Humanities and Social Sciences: ₹10,000/year for M.Phil. and ₹20,500/year for PhD. - Science, Engineering and Technology: ₹12,000/year for M.Phil. and ₹25,000/year for PhD. Other support: - HRA according to the rules of the university/institution. - ₹2,000/month reader/escort assistance for eligible blind and persons-with-disabilities fellows. Payments are made quarterly through Direct Benefit Transfer after the Ministry approves the fellow’s records and required continuation documents.",
