    "officialEligibility": "The applicant must be an Indian national belonging to the Other Backward Classes (OBC), Economically Backward Classes (EBC), or De-notified, Nomadic and Semi-Nomadic Tribes (DNT) categories as notified by Central/State Governments. The candidate must have passed Matriculation (Class 10) or Higher Secondary or higher examination from a recognised Board/University and be enrolled in a recognised post-matric/post-secondary course in an approved institution. Total annual parental/family income from all sources must not exceed ₹2.50 lakh. The scholarship is awarded by the State/UT of permanent domicile. Students pursuing duplicate degrees at the same stage (e.g., B.Sc. after B.A. or M.A. after M.A.) are ineligible. A maximum of two boys per family may avail of this benefit (this restriction does not apply to girl students). Scholarship holders cannot receive another scholarship or stipend simultaneously (except free lodging or ad-hoc book aid). Renewal requires satisfactory progress and minimum 75% attendance.",
    "plainEligibility": "This scholarship is for students from OBC, EBC, or DNT communities whose family earns up to ₹2.5 lakh a year and who are pursuing any recognised course after Class 10 (such as Class 11-12, ITI, polytechnic diploma, BA/B.Sc/B.Com, B.Tech/MBBS, Master's, or PhD) in India. You apply through your home State, cannot receive another scholarship at the same time, and only up to two boys per family can claim it (with no limit on girls).",
    "benefits": "Disbursed directly into the student's Aadhaar-seeded bank account via Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) across four distinct course tiers: - Group 1 (Professional Degree, PG Degree, M.Phil./Ph.D., Post-Doctoral, LL.B., C.A., Commercial Pilot): – Academic Allowance: ₹10,000/year – Tuition Fee: ₹10,000/year – Total: ₹20,000 per annum - Group 2 (Other Professional Courses — Degree, Diploma, Certificate like Pharmacy, Nursing, Paramedical, Hotel Management, Mass Comm, Post-12th ITI/Polytechnic): – Academic Allowance: ₹8,000/year – Tuition Fee: ₹5,000/year – Total: ₹13,000 per annum - Group 3 (General Non-Professional Graduate & Postgraduate Courses — B.A., B.Sc., B.Com., M.A., M.Sc., M.Com., etc.): – Academic Allowance: ₹6,000/year – Tuition Fee: ₹2,000/year – Total: ₹8,000 per annum - Group 4 (All Post-Class 10 Non-Degree Courses — Class 11 & 12 General/Vocational, 3-year Polytechnic Diplomas, Post-10th ITI): – Academic Allowance: ₹5,000/year – Tuition Fee: ₹0 – Total: ₹5,000 per annum (Note: 30% of scheme funds are earmarked for girl students and 5% for persons with disabilities. States may top up allowances from their own budgets).",
