    "notesFlags": "Correction on Income Limit: The raw brief states ₹1 lakh; the updated central guideline has raised the ceiling to ₹2.50 lakh per annum. Correction on Education Level: Covers Class 11 through PhD levels across 4 course groups, not only up to UG. Freeship Card Feature: States can issue a pre-admission digital Freeship Card so low-income students are admitted without upfront payment of tuition/hostel fees. Gender Exemption: The 2-child rule applies only to male children (two boys per family); girl children are exempt and can receive the scholarship without restriction. Funds-Limited Nature: Implemented on a 60:40 Centre-State funding ratio (90:10 for NE/Hilly States); award prioritizes government institutions before private colleges if state funds are constrained.",
