    "incomeLimit": null,
    "officialEligibility": "The applicant must secure admission to an eligible regular ISI degree programme through the Institute’s admission process and meet the programme-specific academic qualifications. For B.Stat (Hons) and B.Math (Hons), the applicant must have completed 10+2 or equivalent with Mathematics and English. For M.Stat, M.Math, MS (QE), MS (QMBA) and MS (LIS), the applicant needs a bachelor’s degree of at least three years in any discipline, subject to programme rules. For M.Tech programmes, the applicant needs the specified engineering/master’s qualification and may be eligible through the GATE/direct-interview route where applicable. Stipends are available to deserving candidates who meet the minimum qualification and continue only if academic performance, attendance and conduct remain satisfactory.",
    "plainEligibility": "This is for students who get admission to selected full-time ISI courses, such as B.Stat, B.Math, M.Stat, M.Math and certain M.Tech programmes. You do not apply separately for this stipend: it comes with eligible admission, but ISI can reduce or stop it if your marks, attendance or conduct fall below its rules.",
