    "lastVerifiedDate": "26 August 2026",
    "researcher": "Manya",
    "notesFlags": "- Benefit update: Your raw project description says ₹3,000–₹12,400/month. The current 2026 ISI admission notice lists ₹5,000/month for B.Stat/B.Math, ₹8,000/month for listed master’s programmes, and ₹12,400/month for the listed M.Tech programmes. The ₹3,000/month amount applies specifically to NE-domicile students in the PG Diploma in Statistical Methods and Analytics programme, not generally to B.Stat/M.Stat/M.Math/M.Tech students. - The general ISI finance page lists older/lower rates—₹3,000 for B.Stat/B.Math, ₹5,000 for listed master’s programmes and ₹8,000 for M.Tech. Because the 2026 admission notice is newer and programme-specific, use the 2026 rates in the Benefits field and preserve this source conflict for a final check. - The stipend is not automatic forever. It is initially awarded at admission and is reviewed by semester according to academic performance, attendance and conduct rules. - If the student receives another scholarship from a government agency, ISI says its stipend will be discontinued. If the other scholarship is received retrospectively, the ISI stipend already paid must be returned. - Under ISI’s continuing-stipend rule, a student receives no stipend in the next semester if any course score is below 35%, if too many course scores are below 45%, if the overall average is below 45%, or if attendance across courses is below 75%. Full stipend generally requires an average composite score of at least 60%; a 45% to below-60% average may result in a half stipend, subject to other conditions. - The older ISI finance page says payments are made for 11 months per academic year and includes a yearly ₹3,000 contingency grant. The 2026 admission notice confirms monthly rates but does not repeat the 11-month/contingency details. Keep these operational details as UNCONFIRMED — needs check for the 2026–27 cohort. - The raw scheme name says “at ISI, Kolkata,” but not all eligible programmes are at Kolkata: B.Math is at Bengaluru; M.Stat starts at Delhi; M.Math is at Kolkata/Delhi; some M.Tech and MS programmes are at other ISI centres. Do not restrict the scheme to Kolkata in the app’s plain-language description.",
