    "name": "Post-Matric Scholarship for Students with Disabilities",
    "ministry": "Department of Empowerment of Persons with Disabilities (DEPwD), Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment, Government of India",
    "categories": [
      "Disability"
    ],
    "categoryLabel": "Disability",
    "educationLevel": "Class 11-12, Diploma, UG, PG",
    "incomeCeiling": "₹2,50,000 per annum or less from all sources of the parent(s)/guardian. For an employed student, the student’s income combined with parent/guardian income must remain within this ₹2.5 lakh ceiling.",
    "incomeLimit": 250000,
    "officialEligibility": "The applicant must be an Indian national with a benchmark disability of 40% or more, holding a valid disability certificate from a competent authority and a UDID card or UDID enrolment. The student must pursue an eligible recognised post-matriculation or post-secondary course in India, up to master’s degree/diploma level, at a recognised institution or university. Parent/guardian income must not exceed ₹2.5 lakh per year. A maximum of two children with disabilities of the same parents may receive benefits; if the second child is a twin, both twins are eligible. The student cannot receive another scholarship or stipend at the same time. A scholarship is available only once for a particular class/year; a student who repeats the class cannot receive it again for that same class. Correspondence, distance and continuing-education students are eligible under this post-matric component.",
    "plainEligibility": "This scholarship is for students with an official disability certificate showing 40% or more disability who are studying after Class 10—such as Class 11–12, a diploma, college degree or master’s course. Your parent/guardian income must be ₹2.5 lakh or less each year, you need a UDID record, and you cannot receive another scholarship or stipend at the same time.",
    "benefits": "- Admission and tuition-fee reimbursement: Up to ₹1,40,000 per year, limited to the actual fee paid/payable. - Compulsory miscellaneous-fee reimbursement: Up to ₹10,000 per year, limited to actual compulsory fees such as library, sports and medical-examination fees. - Maintenance allowance: ₹1,200 per month for hostellers; ₹650 per month for day scholars. - Maintenance allowance is paid for 12 months. - Disability allowance: ₹4,000 per year for students with visual impairment or intellectual disabilities; ₹2,000 per year for students with other types of disabilities. - Book allowance: ₹1,500 per year. - Payment is made through DBT/PFMS to the student’s Aadhaar-linked bank account.",
